-- Stream stages and the pipe connector (SPEC §75 Part B). `Stream[A, K]` is the item effect: a
-- **stage** is a function that performs it, keyed on this declaration and never on the name.
--
-- * `next()` answers an item `inl a`, or `inr k`: the upstream has ended, returning `k`;
-- * `stop()` closes the whole upstream at once, downstream-first, and answers its residual `K`.
--
-- A middle stage also performs `Yield[B]` (`lib/yield.bc`); a sink performs no `Yield`. A stage
-- returns at its stream's end, and a middle stage's result is the `K` of the wire below it.
-- One-item lookahead is a pushback slot the stage holds, not an operation.
--
-- A chain of stream edges (`src >| s₁ >| … `, or `|>` into a stage) is one connector, assembled per
-- chain from the pieces below, each over one stage's or one wire's types (Assembly(n) §1); the
-- elaboration writes only the glue: the tuple of stage states and a dispatching loop.
--
-- A stage's state, `PipeState[L, KN, KY, K]`: `Ready(L)`, a stage not yet run (its loop);
-- `AtNext(KN)`, stored at a `next()` (and at a `stop()`, `AtStop`, at the same type); `AtYield(KY)`,
-- stored at a `yield` (and at a forwarded operation, `AtFwd`, at the same type: SPEC §75
-- (One-frame)); `Ended(K)`, a stage that returned, keeping its unrestricted result. A component a
-- stage does not have is `0`.

include yield

effect Stream[A, K] { ctl next() -> A + K; ctl stop() -> K }

type PipeState[L, KN, KY, K] = L + (KN + (KY + K))

-- handoff_i: wire `i`, from stage `i−1` to stage `i`, at an upstream event `Yield(b, κ)` or
-- `Return(k)` (`B * KY + K`), with stage `i`'s state `S`, which it hands back as it is (stage `i` is
-- `AtNext`, Assembly(n)'s (I5)). Upstream becomes `AtYield(κ)` or `Ended(k)`, and stage `i`'s input
-- is `inl b` or `inr k`.  `[spec §75]`
def pipe_handoff[L, KN, KY, B, K, S] :
    !((B * KY + K) * S => PipeState[L, KN, KY, K] * ((B + K) * S)) =
  !thunkv fun (p : (B * KY + K) * S) ->
    let (e, s) = p;
    case e {
      inl yk ->
        let (b, ky) = yk;
        return ((inr (inr (inl ky)) : PipeState[L, KN, KY, K]), ((inl b : B + K), s))
    | inr k -> return ((inr (inr (inr k)) : PipeState[L, KN, KY, K]), ((inr k : B + K), s))
    }

-- needs row/site-generic defs (#1051). The pieces below force a stored rest, install a stage's
-- sites, or perform at the chain's row, so their types mention the row; a `def` takes value-type
-- parameters only. Their signatures, as Assembly(n) §1 states them, written with the row and site
-- parameters a row-generic definition would take (after `|`: rows; after `;`: sites):
--
--   Rows: `Σ` the chain's outer row, and `CR` the stages' cleanup row within it (each stage
--   operation's cancel row). Sites, connector-local and fresh: `y` the stage's `Yield[B]`, `s` its
--   `Stream[A, K]`, `f` the fresh name of its forwarded operation (`OA ~> OB`), `c` a frame list's
--   cancel region. A stage's own row, inner site first:
--     ROW_i = y.0 cancel[CR] B ~> 1, s.0 cancel[CR] 1 ~> A + K, s.1 cancel[CR] 1 ~> K,
--             f.0 cancel[CR] OA ~> OB, Σ
--   (a source has no `s`, a sink no `y`, a last stage no `f`). Its types:
--     L    = U (nu X. F[ROW_i] (R + U X) & F[CR] 1)                  -- the stage's loop
--     KN   = U (nu XN. (A + K -o F[Σ] EV(XN, KY(XN))) & F[CR, CR] 1)   -- a rest at `next`/`stop`
--     KY   = U (nu XY. (1 -o F[Σ] EV(KN, XY)) & F[CR, CR] 1)           -- at `yield`/forwarded op
--     EV   = (B * KY + (R + L)) + ((KN + KN) + KY)
--            -- Yield(b, κ) | Return(r) | Skip(l) | Next(κ) | Stop(κ) | Fwd(κ)
--     ST   = PipeState[L, KN, KY, R]                                   -- `Ended(r)` at `R`
--     I    = 1 + (A + K)                                               -- the input of a turn
--   (`KN` and `KY` are mutually recursive, written as nested `nu`s; a component a stage lacks
--   is `0`. `OB` is `1` in L1: the rests at `yield` and at a forwarded operation are one type,
--   SPEC §75 (One-frame).)
--
--   def pipe_step[A, K, B, R, OA | Σ, CR; y, s, f] : !(ST * I => EV with Σ)
--     one observation of `L` under the storing clauses at `y`, `s` and `f` (`y` innermost, each
--     rest re-entering the outer sites' clauses), or one resume of the stored rest with `I`;
--   def pipe_stop[A, K, B, R, OA | Σ, CR; y, s, f] : !(ST => 1 with CR)
--     cancels the stored rest; closes `L` when not yet run; `()` at `Ended`;
--   def pipe_with_stop[A, K, B, R, OA, Q | Σ, CR; y, s, f, c] :
--       !(ST * U (1 -o F[c.0 cancel[CR] 1 ~> 1, Σ] Q) => Q with c.0 cancel[CR] 1 ~> 1, Σ)
--     the thunk inside one `unwind` frame whose finaliser is `pipe_stop`: a frame of one of the
--     three frame lists (`close_others_i`, `close_all`, `close_up_i`), each one region at `c`;
--   def pipe_forward[OA, OB | Σ, CR; n.i] : !(OA => OB with n.i cancel[CR] OA ~> OB, Σ)
--     performs the real outer operation `n.i` a non-last stage performed at its fresh name `f`;
--   def pipe_finish[R | Σ] : !(R * U (1 -o F[Σ] 1) => R with Σ)
--     `run`'s end: the others closed by their frame list (the thunk), then `r`.
